  "published": "2026-11-22T18:20:21.513Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Two changes to the OAuth 2.1 authorization server, reaching only an app that registers it. AddOAuthServerEndpoints now returns OAuthServerEndpoints, one builder per endpoint (Registration is null when registration is off), so an app adds a rate limiting policy, a filter or a marker to one endpoint without matching its path; a call chained on the old WebApplication return no longer compiles. IOAuthServerStore gains DeleteExpiredAsync(now, clientsRegisteredBefore), which deletes requests, codes and refresh tokens at or past their ExpiresAt and then the clients registered before the cutoff that nothing left names; a store must implement it. The server calls it in a hosted service of its own every SweepInterval (default 1 hour), with UnusedClientLifetime (default RefreshTokenLifetime) setting the clients' cutoff, so an app removes its own sweep of these rows; a client kept forever before is now deleted once it registered before the cutoff and its last refresh token expired, and must register again to reconnect. See https://github.com/AdamTovatt/easy-reasy/blob/auth-v5.18.0/EasyReasy.Auth/README.md#migration-from-5170",
